{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":262,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T01:50:54.501180Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2881253a-3641-4d7b-a6c1-e09cbbd2d140","comment_uuid":"5c1fc8d0-06e0-4d75-afcb-417d2438f778","author":"79Ig","content":"FINDING (S1 seam scope) + ROUTING. Symptom: the commit-msg hook gates any commit whose staged diff includes DESIGN.md. A --no-ff integration merge of a DESIGN-touching feature branch produces a merge commit that also touches DESIGN.md, so once #96 lands the hook would demand a ratification citation in the MERGE message — but the DESIGN change was already authored + gated + reviewed in-lane; the merge is integration, not a fresh amendment. This is a false-positive, not a dodged true-positive. Route: phase 1b (verification architecture) — the seam's activation scope under-specified authoring-vs-integration. Fix: skip when MERGE_HEAD is present (integration merges carry already-gated authoring commits); documented residual: a DESIGN edit made SOLELY during merge-conflict resolution is not gated (acceptable, low-risk). Seed added: an integration merge touching DESIGN with a bare message is NOT refused, while the authoring-commit seed stays green — the two together pin the corrected scope. Distinguished from escape E-f: routed first, true-positive seed preserved, new seed pins the scope, owned not silent.","created_at":"2026-07-29T01:50:54.480355Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAVXcXgZQrbxcwkD6mQcPKw4cGGtsa4+icizUeuu+bsqf5fpfMt4aD6JvOxn1oL9FukK7FKYNkVycsx0wjOrY6Cw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLRZJBsI