{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":271,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T02:01:42.668436Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1da67425-f44d-40d6-8ba1-2d2ed768de38","comment_uuid":"d7176107-0105-49f3-bb1b-526e94469551","author":"79Ig","content":"PLAN (child of #96, seam S5). Gap: mdatron governs only review-log/**/*.md; the methodology docs that govern mdatron's OWN development (docs/methodology*.md) are themselves ungoverned by mdatron, and no vocabulary registry enforces the naming register (methodology §5: no coined labels / letter-clusters / all-caps tokens). Design: the naming register maps directly onto mdatron's vocabulary family — E0091 (letter+number label clusters outside label_schemes.allow), E0090 (bold-introduced coinages absent from the registry), E0093 (anti-patterns). Dogfood property: to make the methodology docs PASS, their own durable vocabulary (mdatron, vsdd, crosslink; phase handles 1a-2c; seam handles S1-S5) must be REGISTERED in .mdatron/vocabulary.yaml + allowlisted label schemes — which is precisely §5's 'a durable term is a registration act.' Phases: 2a red gate — a planted coinage/bogus letter-cluster in a governed doc is NOT caught today (docs out of scope); 2b — author .mdatron/vocabulary.yaml + bring docs/methodology*.md into file_globs + a route; green when the docs pass (vocabulary registered) AND the planted violation fires; 2c/3/4/5 per the lane. Domain: SE minimum. Standing-doc sweep: DESIGN.md §Five-families + config jurisdiction (#77). Pin dogfood re-run before commit.","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:01:42.549753Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAhz7vBxtSi4vYiC4LBR64ebNoHG6Oo4A1FYkicKqlD/jK9QJ0G6Tj7C0HOrCxz5XFYbg9vntlIi1omB3NfAknCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NI