{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":272,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T02:34:25.128658Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1da67425-f44d-40d6-8ba1-2d2ed768de38","comment_uuid":"6ecb4882-b39a-4dcd-9169-ebf8b7561474","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 3 COLD REVIEW (cold-context adversarial, SE + config-jurisdiction lens) — no blockers; findings routed per practice 2:\nF1 (should-fix, ROUTE→1a design): a zero-match vocabulary_globs silently disables the WHOLE register (E0090-E0094) with no loudness — a mistyped glob makes verify stay clean while scanning nothing; route contrast is E0030 coverage. The scoping contract under-specified zero-match behavior. Disposition: NOT fixed in-lane — a loudness signal is a new warning code (needs code-range + explain page + its own design). Filing a follow-on lane; documenting the sharp edge in DESIGN now. Repo-level risk mitigated by the harden seed below.\nF2 (should-fix, ROUTE→1b verification architecture): both new scoping tests use prose-only fixtures, exercising only the no-frontmatter vocab call site; the frontmatter branch (the review-log's own shape, and the only path where E0094 fires) is unpinned. Disposition: FIX in-lane (phase-5 harden) — add a frontmatter-branch scoping test.\nF3 (nit, ROUTE→1a wording): the rationale says 'E0091 frozen evidence' but the gate scopes the whole family. Disposition: FIX in-lane — correct the config/DESIGN wording.\nF4 (no-issue): confinement weaker than routes but immaterial (post-walk match filter, never widens read surface). No action.\nCore gating + config contract: correct, backward-compatible.","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:34:25.113242Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABApbHb3x+Mah5qQo+826cCL1YgcDmKSAC8jjrsBSabwmOD4+BVd6iJaC8CfaUesT/k/BzexX3r2Cjbkx6ukO2WCg=="},"sign