{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":286,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T02:44:43.669244Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"67c6fa14-5eb9-4657-abd6-904507360757","comment_uuid":"a23a0751-7663-49c9-a26d-0d949a3c10be","author":"79Ig","content":"PLAN (child of #96, session-stop-binding seam). Gap: the hook estate has SessionStart/PreToolUse/PostToolUse hooks but NO Stop hook — the checker-edit dodge (disable/weaken the seam machinery mid-session) is not caught at the session boundary. Design: add .claude/hooks/session-stop.py wired as a Stop hook in .claude/settings.json. It binds the amendment-citation seam's integrity at exit: if .githooks/commit-msg is present in the repo (the seam is expected) but core.hooksPath no longer points at .githooks (disabled) OR the gate tokens were stripped from the hook (weakened), it BLOCKS the clean stop (exit 2) telling Claude to restore the seam; otherwise exits 0 (with a reminder if seam scripts were touched this session). Respects stop_hook_active (no re-block loop). Phases: 2a red gate — no Stop hook, a weakened checker at stop goes uncaught; 2b build + wire; seed (checker-edit escape) — a Rust test in tests/methodology_seams.rs drives session-stop.py in a temp repo across intact/disabled/weakened states. Standing-doc sweep: docs/methodology-enforcement.md seam status + escape-corpus 'checker-edit' row. No mdatron engine change; no DESIGN amendment expected.","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:44:43.647068Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA/bIPSJYWiOiG4SQL2kikI1f+to1BBupog9Hbhdp4U8z1vtfgn2mfIBG83KdYCdLP1pZG2nHAXLovYZhZRDWnDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGKI2VHv1Cpmq79010BjBFLLidL5xaBAt1SFpZC8ywmaQidU0ABIjZ0tSOZ7vOjFPUHJNUsrrZrlbUm9c+zIPw4="}
{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":287,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T02:57:53.382712Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"67c6fa14-5eb9-4657-abd6-904507360757","comment_uuid":"b97fb4d1-d0e9-457f-85fe-3f164eb5fffa","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 3 COLD REVIEW — the seam is INSUFFICIENT as designed; routing before any fix (practice 2). The reviewer proved multiple clean exit-0 dodges of the checker-edit escape the seam is named for:\nBLOCKERS: (1) untrack-the-checker — git rm --cached .githooks/commit-msg makes ls-files fail, hook treats seam as 'not expected', exits 0; the 'tracked=expected' premise is inverted (untracking IS the escape). (2) delete-own-script — .githooks/session-stop.py is UNTRACKED (I never git-added it); deleting it -> settings wrapper [ -f ] false -> exit 0; and docs falsely call it 'tracked/persists' (packaging mismatch). (3) comment-satisfies-token — a gutted 'exit 0' gate that keeps the words DESIGN.md/amendment in a comment passes (substring check defeated). (4) zero-byte checker — 'if body and' skips the weakened-check on empty body -> exit 0.\nSHOULD-FIX: fresh-clone false positive (core.hooksPath is local, unset on clone -> every stop blocks, indistinguishable from malicious unbind); remove-Stop-wiring dodge (hook never inspects settings.json); reworded-checker false positive; the stop_hook_active test runs on an intact repo so it doesn't pin the guard; the block test encodes the fresh-clone false-positive as desired + misses the real bypasses; python3 CI dependency (tests panic, not skip, without python3).\nROUTING → 1a/1b design: a Stop hook cannot robustly self-protect (whatever guards the guard is itself in-repo, editable) — this is a design-level insufficiency, not a patch list. The DURABLE checker-edit catch is the CI seam tests (tests/methodology_seams.rs runs under cargo test in CI): weakening any seam breaks its seeds -> CI red; editing the seeds too is a reviewable diff. The Stop hook's honest role is best-effort SESSION-TIME early-warning for casual disabling, not the primary bind. NOT committing the leaky version; escalating the rescope to the operator.","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:57:53.351965Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA1VP66ajWUGuHk8EsOJgHm2DkZjAOznwLbyEvJCG1NA/JxsOp2rP5Zpb9s8PuegXOIhl6GMKG6DuSItq256asDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA8nhqvDVZImWNEODqhR7qw4PUD2vBYapUQAVb5umJ04ss/mRD/Y92HnGypV9DubV6S5nCYoX/ga/Rm7tFDLogk="}
{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":288,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:20:25.124164Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"67c6fa14-5eb9-4657-abd6-904507360757","comment_uuid":"fcdea940-578f-44e5-bc48-b5dd97d76721","author":"79Ig","content":"RESCOPE per vsdd-cli #819 (operator-relayed, ratified). vsdd-cli formalized enforcement GRADES by distance from the policed agent's reach: detection (reads/reports) -> friction (bypassable local hook that records a deviation) -> CI-backed block (server-side, unskippable, for what CI can independently verify) -> tamper-proof (needs an independent oracle the agent can't author = their corroboration oracle #815; or capability-restriction, a reviewer lacking mutation tools). A Stop hook is grade-2 friction at best (in-repo, can't self-protect — my regress); shipping it as a block asserts enforcement it can't deliver, and it just failed live on their side (Thermite's edit-time gates silently de-wired by a crosslink init settings clobber, uncaught for weeks). DECISION: DROP the session-stop hook; do NOT ship a leaky session-end block. Record checker-edit as caught by: CI-backed block (the seam seeds re-derive integrity over the checker's own wiring — a checker-edit surfaces as CI-red independently of the edited local checker) + friction (the commit-time amendment hook, honest path records the deviation) + owned-bypass for the locally-skippable residual (--no-verify, the deviation is yours to record); the tamper-proof residual (an edit that also fools CI) is named to the corroboration oracle (vsdd #815) as the honest boundary. Methodology note: the directive's 'three mechanisms (engine, git pre-commit, session-stop hook)' updates — the durable third leg is CI-tested integrity, not a session-stop hook. Reframing this lane to deliver the grades model + the drop, not a Stop hook.","created_at":"2026-07-29T04:20:25.109324Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA6gIjKZGcGkd4VnJ5a+OD1j3zHkxitGJldZqnqBUjB0lAlSiT3hDeCIeaI7EI+iB86yVtpw5BSHcmwv8yCc2KBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOpPDa8RJT1zolmGGg4niANVpAZx3x/Isu6O7by6HefqwYvcvrAJuQy74gu3b+EzrkRnIyaMv5PdFJWINerNMAM="}
