{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":296,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T05:14:52.544651Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a0e4b4b2-63f5-41c1-a62d-7713001a66d8","comment_uuid":"9a1b82bb-d7ad-4544-bacc-7dae9e92c9b2","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 1a/1c DECOMPOSITION. #92 is the project's largest lane — DESIGN § 'Verification is fast where it is invoked' + § acceptance 'Incremental agreement' specify a rich contract. Decomposed into 5 sub-lanes:\n\nA. SNAPSHOT SEAM (security-critical) — read inputs once into an immutable snapshot via no-follow handles (Unix openat/O_NOFOLLOW; documented weaker fallback with the check-to-open TOCTOU window); the capture-complete seam (injectable sync point) making mutation-in-flight fixtures deterministic. Domains: SE + SECURITY (confinement/TOCTOU is the load-bearing risk).\n\nB. DEPENDENCY RESOLVER (core algorithm) — the dependent set = transitive closure over three edge kinds: rule-reference (key()/cross-file rule naming, either direction), governance (route governing<->governed, either direction), shared-key (two files coupled via one registry key, naming neither). Oracle = HAND-AUTHORED fixture dependent-sets independent of the resolver. Pure/testable in isolation; no security surface.\n\nC. INCREMENTAL MODE + SOUNDNESS — a changed-file CLI mode verifying changed+dependents; a .mdatron/ change forces whole-tree; the visited-file trace observable (under the escaping discipline). Soundness oracle: incremental result == unrestricted whole-tree result filtered to changed+hand-authored-dependents, no missing/no extra. Depends on A+B.\n\nD. DECLARED BOUNDS + BUDGET DIAGNOSTICS — max input size/file, aggregate snapshot size, concurrent-invocation count, YAML alias/depth, extras-scan depth/entry, global step-and-time budget (covers matching+walking+closure; shared-key cliques make closure superlinear so it's inside the budget by design). Each bound-exceeded is a diagnostic (new codes), no silent degradation. Somewhat independent.\n\nE. CONCURRENCY SAFETY — each invocation owns its snapshot; overlapping runs == serial runs; exercised via the capture-complete seam across overlapping runs. Depends on A.\n\nSuggested order: B (pure resolver) -> A (snapshot+security) -> C (incremental+soundness) -> D (bounds) -> E (concurrency). Each is a full fix-lane (red gate, domain review incl. SECURITY for A, harden). Also resolves DESIGN's index-persistence OPEN block boundary and records the first latency actual (0.65s/178-files/0.1.0) in the cost ledger when C lands. This is a multi-session effort; recommend building sub-lane by sub-lane with operator merge gates. NOT starting implementation until the decomposition shape is ratified.","created_at":"2026-07-29T05:14:52.530689Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAVXbn/8aBWShQOm3ZMOf5nGOltvWobo9JtL1gokOJHeBKFub4/Bx3f9jSAyli1vfjslCQomhMWuvE7ygUAopZBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFDBq6XohjiXaXaMqoRg6gs+yGSOSEBhmXjKRTRsGnlF8H1giFrP0Ud10OjEoxKZDFHEbZCHwNgFunhfmMK/+gI="}
