{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":308,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T05:24:44.486430Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f00730f0-5883-4ad4-9ae0-9a665b2baa0b","comment_uuid":"5badc1e2-36c1-4e1a-84a5-e0209b281812","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 1a/1b/1c DESIGN (sub-lane B of #92).\n\nEDGE DERIVATION (all edges undirected — DESIGN says 'either direction'):\n1. GOVERNANCE — from LoadedRoutes: for each route (files glob, governed_by), every file F matching the glob has an edge F<->governed_by. Available today from route.rs; no new infra.\n2. SHARED-KEY + RULE-REFERENCE — require PROVENANCE the current index lacks. Index today is key->Value with NO record of which source file produced each key (index.rs:46, entries: BTreeMap<String,Value>). Need key->{contributing files} per index. Then:\n   - shared-key edge: two files contributing the same key value to the same index -> edge (they name neither each other).\n   - rule-reference edge: a rule with context C that calls key(index,...) connects files-of-context-C <-> source-files-of-that-index. Requires walking each Rule's Expr tree for key() calls to find which indices a context references (expr.rs Function nodes).\n\nRESOLVER INTERFACE: build a DepGraph once (from routes + provenance index + per-rule key() analysis); dependents(changed) = transitive closure (BFS) over the undirected edge set. The .mdatron/-change->whole-tree rule and mode selection belong to sub-lane C, not B — B is the pure graph.\n\nVERIFICATION ARCH (1b) — hand-authored fixtures, dependent sets authored independent of the resolver (DESIGN acceptance): (a) 3-file transitive chain; (b) shared-key conflict (two files, same key, naming neither); (c) governance edge both directions; (d) rule-reference both directions. Each fixture asserts resolver output == hand-authored set, no missing/no extra.\n\n1c DECOMPOSITION of B: B1 provenance-aware index (key->files), B2 per-rule key()-reference extraction, B3 graph builder + closure, B4 the hand-authored fixture suite. B1 ripples through Index consumers, so it is the load-bearing sub-step.\n\nCHECKPOINT: design complete + branch cut. Recommend implementing in a fresh focused session — B needs new provenance infra + expression analysis + graph code, and this session has run very long; quality-first says start the implementation clean rather than deep in context.","created_at":"2026-07-29T05:24:44.446223Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA7Hv9pAD+LIyEFDT4jZ8ncmz/9kzZJOCBhC0YhA8QnMwEVkNxolrk4ukCjwLuw3VMhcCOxZ4rre30prOftlVNCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD6RfFeL2B6NzAg1KpkwW5TEGXh1+R9RYtOQSAKL3tQSYHh0DNmoTmoZ9w7HOclPcrR0aOsss0jnVPWHmIOGwAY="}
