{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":312,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T05:52:17.602708Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f00730f0-5883-4ad4-9ae0-9a665b2baa0b","comment_uuid":"5211023d-0753-49fa-9262-7a72982d1f0e","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 3 COLD REVIEW — no blockers to the design, but 3 genuine MISSING-EDGE (unsoundness) classes reachable from adopter inputs; routing before fix (practice 2). Clean: walk_expr recursion (exhaustive, no wildcard), provenance last-wins + sources completeness, shared-key clique, rule-reference-to-all-sources, governance breadth.\nF1 (missing edge, ROUTE→1a): a key() appearing ONLY in a rule's message {{...}} is never scanned (interpolate_message evaluates it) — the design under-specified the scan surface. FIX in-lane: scan rule.message slots too.\nF2 (missing edge, ROUTE→1a): key() with a non-literal first arg (dynamic index name via a let-binding/field) is silently dropped, but the evaluator evaluates args[0]. FIX in-lane: a dynamic key() makes the rule reference ALL indices (conservative, no-missing-edge).\nF3 (missing edge, ROUTE→1b): governed_by is used as a raw graph node while every other node is confine-normalized (no leading ./), so 'governed_by: ./DESIGN.md' attaches to a distinct node and the governance edge silently fails to connect. FIX in-lane: normalize governed_by via confine_lexically.\nF4 (test gap, ROUTE→1b): let-binding scan untested; no edge-kind composition/diamond/self-ref; F1/F2 uncovered. FIX in-lane: add those seeds.\nF5 (nit): DESIGN 'keyed rule' phrase in shared-key def == registry index (key() is the sole cross-file mechanism); adding a clarifying note. All fixes land before merge.","created_at":"2026-07-29T05:52:17.587724Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAYooW7SwvvaOChKIOpEcUC8