{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":328,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:22:45.418875Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"defb3290-053e-4af9-989f-daf56c87410a","comment_uuid":"3586b80f-6c48-4bde-8a00-c6f414ab38c4","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 1a/1b DESIGN (sub-lane C of #92). Incremental mode + the soundness oracle, built on the #100 resolver.\n\nSOUNDNESS ARGUMENT (why the fast path equals whole-tree-filtered): verify_file is PER-FILE — every finding it emits is located at that file. So running verify_file only on the scope files yields EXACTLY the whole-tree findings located in scope; no scope-located finding is missed, none extra. Whole-run checks (pin::check, vocab registry W0044, W0043) run fully (cheap) and are filtered to scope by finding location. A .mdatron/ change forces whole-tree (DESIGN); .mdatron-located findings (route-load, W0043, W0044) are never in a governed-file scope, so they filter out in incremental — consistent with 'filtered to changed+dependents'.\n\nMECHANISM: refactor verify_report into run(config, changed: Option<&Path>). When changed is Some and not under .mdatron/: walk once, read each governed file's schema_class (a light pre-pass), build DepGraph (#100), scope = {changed} ∪ dependents(changed); the per-file loop skips files not in scope; the final pass filters findings to scope-located (rel-path membership). Whole-tree path (changed=None) is unchanged. New public verify_incremental(config, changed) -> IncrementalReport { report, visited } exposes the visited-file trace (scope). CLI wiring (a --changed flag) is a thin follow-on within this lane.\n\nVERIFICATION ARCH (1b): the soundness oracle as a property test — for a fixture repo with cross-file rules, incremental(changed).findings == whole_tree().findings filtered to visited, no missing/no extra, over several changed files; plus a .mdatron/-change forces whole-tree; plus the visited trace stays within the hand-authored dependent scope. Red gate first.","created_at":"2026-07-29T06:22:45.383551Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA3yV1f3BVl1Fs8kngixXICDRMSrfRCZHYt4iqNrP9HBsV5TU9B+syT+BjBEZRT/GD2KMJ4GN8ziHdkKoNm8PmCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJCroeXVGcLkhStrn6yTBZhCFLlkRWew9pYaLs9sku9nBAP+PVDjCLhZtFGN7687wT2TvYUs9w0D2qfwMycGSg0="}
{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":329,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:48:56.587534Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"defb3290-053e-4af9-989f-daf56c87410a","comment_uuid":"1243d6f3-e094-438e-8d95-d4a907dc7d2c","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 3 COLD REVIEW — 3 blockers + should-fixes; routing before fix (practice 2). Dimensions 2 (whole-run scope-file findings) + 5 (double-parse) clean.\n\nB1 (pin findings dropped, ROUTE→1a/DESIGN): pin::check locates E0061/E0062 at .mdatron/pins.yaml, never in a governed-file scope, so the location filter drops them — a stale pin on a governed file that whole-tree BLOCKS reports clean under --changed. This defeats the pin attention loop in exactly the hook mode DESIGN designates as its trigger. But DESIGN's OWN soundness definition ('findings locatable in changed+dependents') also excludes pins.yaml, so it's sound-to-the-letter — this is a DESIGN-contract tension (pin findings should relocate to the governed file, or incremental must special-case them), needs operator + owned process. DISPOSITION: loud limitation notice in-lane now + route the proper fix; NOT silently shipped.\n\nB2 (circular oracle, FIX in-lane): assert_incremental_sound derives 'expected' from the engine's own visited set, so it can't catch a too-few-dependents resolver — the exact self-referential-oracle failure DESIGN Evidence records. FIX: rewrite with a HAND-AUTHORED scope independent of the resolver.\n\nB3 (non-canonical/symlinked --changed collapses scope -> silent clean, FIX in-lane): rel_to_root strips the CANONICAL root from a RAW path; a symlinked root (/tmp->/private/tmp on macOS) or absolute non-prefixed path fails strip_prefix, stays absolute, dependents()=empty, walk skips all -> clean while whole-tree finds real findings. Same root cause = the .mdatron/-bypass (absolute .mdatron path doesn't start_with '.mdatron' -> verified incrementally). FIX: canonicalize the changed path; force whole-tree / error if it doesn't resolve under root or isn't governed.\n\nSF4 (no validation --changed is a real governed file, FIX in-lane): a typo -> scope={typo}, walk matches nothing -> clean 'success'. FIX: error loudly if changed resolves to no governed file.\n\nSF6 (escape_trace_path diverges from diagnostic discipline, ROUTE→follow-on): injection-SAFE (escapes all Cc + U+2028/9) but re-implements escaping with a divergent format (\\u{000a} vs diagnostic \\xNN) instead of routing through diagnostic::safe_display. Minor consistency; follow-on.","created_at":"2026-07-29T06:48:56.238597Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA21KtZrturpvYhr/NM5GtUh1AGDakgfsrEbgz4DigmbZ/99NfISAzLL2IeNO9ZAnVRiDyx2NyPEzQg6RFjvDoBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAsONOZ0KwVTGXqMb9Ha1AMQAbEulYW+UKUToaL2Mzf/7bXsxRK4GMQkbRs4drVryTtzZEYgLhsViEIpmf8IPws="}
{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":330,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:57:58.130268Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8368834a-bc3c-4500-a10a-7dad88e1c9ff","comment_uuid":"3d28ab9f-fca0-49c3-bc00-0cc3e61bda89","author":"79Ig","content":"CASE TEXTS RECEIVED (vsdd-cli relay). Source: vsdd-cli rounds #684 (e61f28e5), #705 (026564ee), #710. Two lenses (DR+SA) converged on #684. The three verbatim E0094 drift cases for fixture intake:\n\nCASE 1 — plain count drift from disk. Site: installed-artifact-manifest.md:83. Claim: '27 members / 17 domain prompts'. Basis: count of installed prompt files on disk. Disk actual: '28 members / 18 domain prompts (+ 10 primers)'. Corrected to '28 members / 18 domain prompts + 10 primers' with a verified-against-disk citation.\n\nCASE 2 — decomposed-count drift (total AND component). Site: economics-data.md:35. Claim: '17: 15 role + 2 meta'. Disk actual: '18: 16 role + 2 meta'. Both total (17->18) and role component (15->16) drifted while arithmetic stayed internally consistent (15+2=17) — a checker that only re-adds stated components MISSES it; components must be checked against the basis. Corrected to '18 (16 role + 2 meta)'.\n\nCASE 3 — unperformable basis (the high-value case). Stage A (#684): claim 'seven core role domains'; tier basis yields six — wrong number. Stage B (#705): fix rewrote to 'six core role domains' = the tier field's own count, BUT no field named tier carries a domain count (only tier_effort_defaults) — number right, basis dangling. Stage C (#710): the 'six' cited installed prompts, but that basis verifies only the 18-total — the six-member subset is enumerated nowhere. Corrected (#710): name the six inline (software-engineer, security, ux, quality-engineer, solution-owner, solution-architect) — count+membership verifiable against the tier-marked installed prompts. WHY IT MATTERS: distinguishes 'the number is wrong' from 'the number's stated verification path doesn't resolve' — a digit-comparison passes Stage B (six IS the count) while the doc stays unverifiable. The performable-basis half is the harder, higher-value part of E0094. Ready for fixture intake.","created_at":"2026-07-29T06:57:58.100827Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABATGNmVTRJU8zN+1rY/ghnOAYpLQAdLjnFKbc+yd7M7zJqMXrCJeuiTsJUGjuTewqBOSceAg3cLqGdPSqy+G5RAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKxLI6WXnGQjyLQnNPckYT6BseqcT6zuUO2eQlCGKx8SHcj+Nd39hs2YPaobpCUMXBO99y2luNasyRM5TqVfyAw="}
{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":331,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:58:18.870957Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"fea9b536-a072-4342-afe0-0a87fe5ca8bd","comment_uuid":"ac1f1011-972b-4845-bfb7-b6a7f254fb13","author":"79Ig","content":"vsdd-cli 0.1.0->0.3.0 UPGRADE FEEDBACK (relay, from the actual flip 2026-07-28). VERDICT: clear-to-publish is DEFERRED until they've built on v0.3.0 across a couple slices — this is adoption feedback, NOT the final #48 go/no-go. HOLD #48 on their account; NOTHING BLOCKING found in adoption. 'Don't wait on us if you'd rather ship on your own judgment.'\n\nWorked well: (1) E0080 jurisdiction path — migration was config.yaml alone, message pointed straight at the fix; (2) mdatron init idempotency + adopter/managed split (standout — on a mirror of their 0.1.x layout, init added only the missing managed manifest.yaml and preserved their adopter-owned config.yaml hash-checked; E0060 refusal on managed hand-edits 'exactly right'); (3) families report (#90) on --json; tag hygiene (0.3.0 bump) correct; their pre-commit ran v0.3.0 verify live during the flip — clean.\n\nFEEDBACK / QUESTIONS (candidate enhancements — propose filing each):\n- (A, load-bearing) families active/inactive SEMANTICS. On a clean run (0 findings) they get schema=active but vocabulary=inactive EVEN THOUGH vocabulary_globs is set. So 'active' isn't 'produced findings' (run was clean) and 'inactive' isn't 'not configured' (vocab IS configured). For families to serve as the un-invoked-mechanism audit signal they asked for, document precisely what active vs inactive mean — ideally a TRI-STATE separating 'invoked, ran, nothing to act on (clean)' from 'not invoked / not applicable'. [NOTE: this smells like a real bug — vocabulary should report active when vocabulary.yaml is present; investigate whether from_supplied(vocab.is_some()) is being overridden.]\n- (B) init discoverability on 0.1.x upgrades. They hand-built .mdatron/ under 0.1.x and never knew to run init; verify is clean without manifest.yaml, so nothing surfaced the missing managed manifest. Suggest a migration note or a verify hint when .mdatron/ predates the managed-manifest layout.\n- (C) pin (#84) baseline. 'mdatron pin' reports 'no pin record (pins.yaml absent)'; init doesn't scaffold it. Is pins.yaml part of the recommended adoption baseline or an advanced opt-in? Clarify in adoption docs.","created_at":"2026-07-29T06:58:18.851903Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABARiCCZqz/Z4GvblccOHMgwrIets0qq0MhmOQOKuorZFjUKSP1OA66d8A9M9BMGPXJf3EsL3bgL89dZRFD5G9ODw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCKuF4glZJk0s+VWvceJ9jYvJFNdJPaLriMfHzdIb+LDvGGBU5g2GZLi1v1kc4znAJZStoo/0N01aVQyZCX1NwQ="}
