{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":344,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T07:23:47.017704Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ca2e6c21-f9fd-4751-9ca4-24ef840c72e0","comment_uuid":"90a0d369-0dd3-4dc9-9584-62b186c1dd6a","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 1a/1b/1c DESIGN (sub-lane A of #92, SECURITY-critical). Composition: SE + SECURITY (confinement/TOCTOU is the load-bearing risk).\n\nGAP FOUND: verify_file reads governed files via raw std::fs::read_to_string (verify.rs:606) — bypassing the confined no-follow handle path (confine::open_confined, openat/O_NOFOLLOW) that index.rs and pin.rs already use. So the MAIN per-file check has neither the confinement guarantee (a symlinked governed-file component is followed) nor the read-once immutability. read_schema_class (the #102 pre-pass) reads raw too.\n\nDESIGN CONTRACT (§ Verification is fast): each invocation reads inputs ONCE through validated no-follow handles into an IMMUTABLE snapshot; all checks run on snapshot bytes; mutations after capture don't affect the in-flight run. Unix openat/O_NOFOLLOW is the handle read; the fallback (per-component symlink-check + open) has a documented check-to-open TOCTOU window, tolerated only where no openat surface exists. A capture-complete seam (injectable sync point) makes mutation-in-flight fixtures deterministic.\n\nDECOMPOSITION:\n- A1 (foundation): build a read-once Snapshot (rel -> content) via open_confined at run start; reroute verify_file + read_schema_class to read from the snapshot, not the FS. Closes the raw-read confinement gap + gives immutability. Mostly plumbing + a security improvement.\n- A2 (determinism): the capture-complete seam (injectable sync point) + mutation-in-flight fixtures (mutate at the seam, assert the run reports against snapshot bytes).\n- A3 (security acceptance + REVIEW): check-then-swap seed against confinement; overlapping invocations with a mutation between starts each report against own snapshot; adverse-filename in the visited trace escaped. SECURITY domain review of the whole snapshot/TOCTOU surface.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: A is security-critical + needs the SECURITY domain review; build it as a FOCUSED effort (this session has run extraordinarily long, and TOCTOU-sensitive code is exactly where session-depth risk bites). Design recorded; branch cut.","created_at":"2026-07-29T07:23:47.002155Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA555JyuYu7/N7+RTaZX7bmS6F+8Yy2ppRKTtG4oTg8CMuazBT83kHOQ124j/AsLS0yHK9ApTICh83z8XvpcVSBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPk7Q/vZp1ZUCSdyzPFWI11pzGs4HVJUpunPQIZjo9MpDuB/+UV9lBfZvqDfh0yhzp/cl/Ybcf74Gpj/ddSfnQ4="}
{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":345,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T07:42:27.181877Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ca2e6c21-f9fd-4751-9ca4-24ef840c72e0","comment_uuid":"564c0418-b56c-40d5-bcd5-3e97929e215a","author":"79Ig","content":"PHASE 3 SECURITY COLD REVIEW — 1 blocker + should-fixes. CLEAN: governed-file BODY read TOCTOU closed (open_confined returns the validated handle, that handle is read, no re-open by path); symlink refusal complete at every component (openat O_NOFOLLOW per-component); catalog tests unaffected.\n\nA (BLOCKER — contract not met): the snapshot covers ONLY the governed-file body read. IndexRegistry::build reads index sources BEFORE the snapshot; pin::check + cite::check_file read fresh from disk AFTER the seam. So 'all checks run against snapshot bytes' is FALSE — a concurrent mutation gives an inconsistent cross-check view within one run (rules evaluate body version B against an index built from A; pin certifies restored bytes Y while Layer-1/2 validated X). This is the CORE of sub-lane A's immutable-snapshot deliverable; achieving it fully requires unifying index/pin/cite reads through one snapshot built BEFORE any check. DISPOSITION: what's built (confined body read + symlink refusal + seam) is a real security fix but is PARTIAL — I will CORRECT THE OVERCLAIM in the code (not claim full immutability) and route the full snapshot-unification as the remaining A work for an owned decision (big cross-module refactor).\n\nB (should-fix): the seam covers only the body map; pin/cite read post-seam so 'deterministic via seam' is false for them. The immutability test only exercises the schema path (no pins/citations) — reframe honestly.\n\nC (should-fix, DoS): a non-UTF8/unreadable governed file -> VerifyError::Io aborts the WHOLE run (zero findings for the tree) — a denial-of-verification lever, and inconsistent with the symlink E0012 skip. FIX in-lane: a localized finding (like E0001), not a pipeline kill.\n\nD (should-fix, silent regression): a glob-matched governed file whose rel isn't lexically confinable (file_globs with ..) is silently skipped with NO finding (pre-#103 verified it via raw read). FIX in-lane: emit a finding, never a silent drop.\n\nE (should-fix, DoS) -> ROUTE to sub-lane D: no per-file/aggregate snapshot size bound (DESIGN lists these as declared bounds); incremental reads the whole tree into memory. Bounds are literally sub-lane D's scope.\n\nF (nit) -> follow-on: E0012 explain page is key-source-specific; reused for governed files (doc muddiness, no test breaks). Generalize the page across families.","created_at":"2026-07-29T07:42:27.159003Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAoDqlDSI5xnyfmySaChUNVB3a2eFhfdA9oUINm1TmBXbsQ45enmSIktcgKhGcoyJyjyWuv3uYD8aG5dNTZ3JmBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGK/bw7lAwdAkXkBo9PagduG5Ccaqkqbv5Mpduhe2q3Yj+oVVYUUrV2HIyiUPutOqEzFunOksHh86VIhqITrggw="}
