{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":349,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T07:55:22.772537Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"18545077-3dbb-4401-847d-c6b4bdbe7d78","comment_uuid":"589bedde-7450-4981-ac08-3dd3246f0fff","author":"79Ig","content":"vsdd-cli v0.3.0 diagnostic-efficacy review (6 domain lenses, each reproduced against live v0.3.0). STRONG: error[CODE]/-->file:line:col/=note/=help/=explain shape is agent-parseable; --json -q clean single-line; MDATRON-namespace explain pages model-grade; exit-code discipline (0/1/2) CI-legible; explain arg-parsing injection-hardened; quoted[] recovers values; output-version 1.0.0->1.1.0 additive.\n\nTHROUGH-LINE CONCERN: mdatron can't distinguish 'checked N files, all clean' from 'checked nothing' — the audit-signal gap. 10 substantive items:\n1. files_checked is a MISNOMER — counts files WITH findings, not files validated (1 valid->0, clean repo->0); a clean corpus and an empty jurisdiction emit an identical envelope. Fix: true files_walked/in_scope/routed count.\n2. Missing .mdatron/schemas/ -> silent false-clean (ok, exit 0, 'clean'); only families.schema:inactive tells. Contradicts DESIGN. Fix: fail or emit a finding.\n3. Unroutable schema_class silently UNVALIDATED — a made-up schema_class on a garbage file -> 0 findings (W0040 only catches MISSING frontmatter). Fix: diagnose frontmatter that routes to no schema.\n4. families is UNFALSIFIABLE — inactive conflates not-configured with configured-but-didn't-run; doesn't track pattern execution (pattern rules fire while route:inactive; vocabulary_globs set but vocabulary:inactive). Fix: tri-state + reason; map pattern rules to families. [overlaps #48-A]\n5. MDATRON-E0080 masks all findings + overloaded across >=5 senses with one explain page; error_count stays 0 on failure. Fix: split codes or add pipeline_error:{code,kind,note} / top-level checked:false.\n6. --json --quiet (documented CI mode) DROPS the failure reason on pipeline failure (findings:[], no reason; the note is stderr-only, -q suppresses). Fix: carry the reason into the envelope.\n7. VSDD-namespace explain is a DEAD-END — every VSDD finding advertises 'mdatron explain VSDD-...' which the same binary rejects. Fix: resolve VSDD pages or stop advertising.\n8. VSDD pattern-message interpolation is BROKEN — {{$self.x}} renders literally as {$self.x} (values only in quoted[]); in --compact the value elides under 512 while the placeholder survives. Affects all E0201-E0212. Fix: interpolate; budget the value ahead of the template in compact.\n9. Diagnostic-content INJECTION — adopter bytes reach the agent surface/quoted[].content with no untrusted flag in JSON (only the > convention). Fix: mark quoted adopter content origin:'adopter'/trusted:false.\n10. Jurisdiction/--files self-audit BYPASS — narrowing config.yaml file_globs or --files silently shrinks the corpus (exit 0, no warning); E0060 says jurisdiction edits 'do not drift.' Fix: warn on zero-match globs; record a jurisdiction hash; flag jurisdiction shrink.\n\nMEDIUM/LOW: DESIGN 'See also' links resolve to files adopters don't have + #summary anchor mismatches; E0080 stale 'v0.1.x init will scaffold' framing; --json without -q double-emits (~1.7x tokens); pattern-rule location coarse (:1 col 0) vs schema's precise :4:8; explain needs full code + has no --list; --compact truncates mid-sentence; the promised output.schema.json 'absent' [NOTE: we DID publish schema/mdatron-output.schema.json in #90 — verify vsdd's expected path/name] + no contract test [we added contract-stability CI in #90 — verify].\n\nCluster: items 1-5,10 are the audit-signal gap (prove-you-checked); 7-9 are VSDD-consumer surface (explain resolution, interpolation, injection-marking); 6 is the CI envelope. Needs decomposition + prioritization.","created_at":"2026-07-29T07:55:22.757516Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA0L9hXReu8hp38Kg/zUh8w5jpuqooJi3lufFYcHVkchCqHpz8Ut1AORLjQ44dgR0BC/VdjqJevwyXWJtNNZYtCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPoMmd+aZwUbagkYVYHl3LwNBUqnh7kKNMOCE+44dGr/kqK4hnPbGhHeD0t/vtKkGuUCjgyxpS1gITRBHQmp7gI="}
{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":350,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T08:00:00.383385Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ca2e6c21-f9fd-4751-9ca4-24ef840c72e0","comment_uuid":"7c227e91-07ed-41c9-b980-ef9c82a10223","author":"79Ig","content":"PARTIAL merged to main (operator-ratified 2026-07-29): the confined no-follow body read + symlink refusal + capture-complete seam. #103 STAYS OPEN for the full immutable-snapshot unification (security review Finding A: index/pin/cite reading from one snapshot) — to be taken FRESH LATER with the security review front-loaded (operator ruling 2026-07-29). The Snapshot scaffolding was set aside; the design + the byte-snapshot approach are recorded above for the fresh start. Also carry the fixed should-fixes forward: C (non-UTF8 -> per-file finding, not whole-run abort), E (bounds -> sub-lane D), F (E0012 explain generalization).","created_at":"2026-07-29T08:00:00.366401Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAetqiCGBhlbRXpMYoZKRJDF5C3G43TsKBHQhwZo3NkbA//kaKIjVAElRkOFJ88dxM2TS3I7SqLkZyqQO+qczwCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKJWGGOMZIHDJANXVVFKIOPOhrNsnWC/b0at9Pn/HdpHaOF/VfuDUXJDtoEScT14htb072BseiXOFCdzMJLAVQQ="}
{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":351,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T08:00:34.823141Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"18545077-3dbb-4401-847d-c6b4bdbe7d78","comment_uuid":"0c1b23c9-3ca5-41a4-a85f-3936053a111e","author":"79Ig","content":"VERIFICATION + DECOMPOSITION for the fresh start.\n\nTwo 'absent' items RESOLVED: schema/mdatron-output.schema.json EXISTS (published #90, 3581 bytes) and the contract test envelope_validates_against_published_schema is live in src/output.rs. vsdd's 'output.schema.json absent / no contract test' is a DISCOVERABILITY gap — they looked for output.schema.json; ours is schema/mdatron-output.schema.json behind a versioned $id. Fix is docs/discoverability (point adopters at the path, or alias the name), not implementation.\n\nLIGHTWEIGHT DECOMPOSITION (each item likely its own fix-lane; sequence TBD in the fresh design pass):\n- W1 AUDIT-SIGNAL (the through-line, vsdd-rated load-bearing across all 6 lenses): #1 files_checked -> true files_walked/in_scope/routed counts; #2 missing schemas/ -> finding not silent-clean; #3 unroutable schema_class -> finding; #4 families tri-state + reason + map pattern-rule execution to families (overlaps #48-A); #10 jurisdiction shrink -> warn on zero-match globs + record a jurisdiction hash. RECOMMEND STARTING HERE.\n- W2 CI ENVELOPE: #5 E0080 overloaded -> split codes or pipeline_error:{code,kind,note}/checked:false; #6 --json --quiet carries the failure reason into the envelope.\n- W3 VSDD-CONSUMER SURFACE: #7 resolve/redirect VSDD-namespace explain (dead-end); #8 fix {{...}} pattern-message interpolation (+ compact value budgeting); #9 mark quoted adopter content origin:'adopter'/trusted:false (SECURITY / diagnostics-are-a-trust-surface, overlaps DESIGN).\n- W4 POLISH (medium/low): See-also link resolution + anchors; E0080 'v0.1.x init' framing; --json-without-q double-emit; pattern-rule location precision (:1 col 0 -> :line:col); explain --list + full-code UX; --compact mid-sentence truncation; schema discoverability (above).\nStanding focus per operator 2026-07-29; taken fresh.","created_at":"2026-07-29T08:00:34.809972Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAjWkI1wXf0VWa6VrWBgz51+2FB1Q6B8MbqjobR/szxILF0LYxJdith918hhuFhvdaYrG/lZc/kuS3UAkBjhfbAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIw54avbGt2gAQUS4djT53JbJCDVMjaIg3WpQGpKf4xXXplhulX1f3hAORXCgH/d4A5sSEu1N24LhTmYlHSFrAs="}
